  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Living the call of Pope Francis Laudato Si&#x2019; Encyclical  in the AMECEA Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is designed to advance the commitment of AMECEA and its pastoral agents in caring for the environment. AMECEA through its strategic plan for 2014-2024 prioritizes Integral Ecology as a concern for the entire region. Through this project, AMECEA shall have a series of activities and advocacy interventions, with an aim of positive formation of the youth, women, children, clergy, men, religious men and women at all levels and further inform the policy makers in the Church on what needs to be done to ensure sustainable care for our common home. 
The Knowledge acquired will empower the people within the AMECEA region to have skills to care for the environment. The National Conferences will use the AMECEA Laudato Si&#x2019; implementation guidelines to influence activities towards the care for mother earth. In its implementation, AMECEA will work through the National Conferences to reach dioceses, selected parishes and the faithful at the grassroots level. Through the SCCs, men, women, PWD and the youth will participate in the care for our common home and strengthen the governance for integral development of the people of God and people of good will in the AMECEA region.</narrative>
  </description>
